            <ArticleTitle>Pediatric chest pain: case report of a malignant cause.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>43-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Pediatric chest pain is not an uncommon presenting complaint in the emergency department. Although the majority of cases are benign, the authors report on a patient with a fetal case of myocarditis. A discussion of myocarditis and its management as well as differential diagnosis is included.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
